{
  "name": "fusion",
  "after": "first_duel_play",
  "description": "first_duel_play, then EVOSEG: the Fusion Shop of Flame City. The shop opens only after five CPU duels (Beginner City's two arenas, or Flame City's), whose shuffles and choices follow rand(), whose position differs between the emulator and the port; so on the world map a fixture writes the progress (write_mem: areaScriptFlags r12, r13, r283; scriptFlags bit 9, the shop fusing up to level 3; one ExVeemon and one Stingmon, an EVO_FUSION_RECIPES pair whose result draws no rand()), Beginner City is entered and left once (its script loads and saves the flags), and the marker walks to Flame City. In the shop: Card Fusion of ExVeemon and Stingmon (the Yes/No dialog, the fusion cutscene with its banner, issue #44, and the RECEIVED! result), then Partner Fusion of Veemon with the new Paildramon (the partner list and status, a Digi-Part reward), then out and back to Flame City's menu. Every press waits on the state that takes it: SAISEG's SAI_AREA (waitingForCross +0x120, mode +0x10E, choicePhase +0x81, choiceMode +0x82, choiceCursor +0x83) and SAI_WORLD_MAP (state +0x403, nodeIndex +0x406); EVOSEG's EVO_FUSION (swapState +0xB9, fusionType +0xBA, scriptState +0xBB, typeChoiceOpen +0xBC, partnerListOpen +0xBE, step +0xC1, previewOpen +0xC3, pickSlot +0xC4, resultKind +0xC5, cutscene +0xC7, textTyping +0xC9), EVO_DIALOG (animDone +0x41, choice +0xA5, closed +0xB4), EVO_CURSOR_CARD, EVO_CUTSCENE_STEP, EVO_BANNER_FADE.",
  "max_frames": 20000,
  "default_timeout": 3000,
